# Sitecore AI — required viewport widths

When building or updating the **TSX creation skill/code** for Sitecore AI (section → React/TSX, `*.definition.ts`, import pipelines, responsive previews), support these viewport widths (Pages / Sitecore AI device presets):

| Label | Width |
|-------|-------|
| Mobile | **370px** |
| Tablet Portrait | **768px** |
| Desktop Small | **1024px** |
| Flexible | no fixed width (user-resizable; do not hardcode a px width) |
| Desktop Regular | **1280px** |
| Desktop Large | **1536px** |

## Usage notes

- Prefer these widths for capture alignment, component responsive CSS, and any generated preview/test harnesses tied to Sitecore AI.
- Do not invent alternate “standard” breakpoints (e.g. 375 / 1440) when the task is Sitecore AI TSX creation unless the user overrides.
- **Flexible** is a mode, not a fixed breakpoint — keep layout fluid; still ensure the fixed presets above look correct.
